CT_OFFERED_SUMMARY.NUM_ENROLLED_STUDENTS\n- responsible faculty name: TIP_SUBJECT_OFFERED.RESPONSIBLE_FACULTY_NAME\n- offer department name: TIP_SUBJECT_OFFERED.OFFER_DEPT_NAME\n- degree-granting subjects: SIS_COURSE_DESCRIPTION.IS_DEGREE_GRANTING\n- enrolled students: SUBJECT_OFFERED_SUMMARY.NUM_ENROLLED_STUDENTS\n- subjects offered by that department: SUBJECT_OFFERED_SUMMARY.OFFER_DEPT_CODE\n\n## Join Keys\n- SIS_COURSE_DESCRIPTION.COURSE <-> SIS_SUBJECT_CODE.COURSE_NUMBER\n- SIS_COURSE_DESCRIPTION.COURSE <-> SUBJECT_OFFERED_SUMMARY.COURSE_NUMBER\n- LIBRARY_RESERVE_MATRL_DETAIL.SUBJECT_ID <-> TIP_DETAIL.SUBJECT_ID\n- TIP_DETAIL.SUBJECT_ID <-> TIP_SUBJECT_OFFERED.SUBJECT_ID\n\n## Question\nFor each department and each library reserve material detail with material status key equal to 'U' for subjects offered by that department, what are the department code, department name, the variance of the total number of units for degree-granting subjects with more than 0 enrolled students, the average number of enrolled students for those subjects, the enrollment category (classified as 'HIGH_ENROLLMENT' if the average enrolled students is at least 20% higher than the overall average, 'LOW_ENROLLMENT' if at least 20% lower, or 'AVERAGE' otherwise), the library course instructor key, library reserve catalog key, term code, subject ID, the tip material key, tip material status key, tip ISBN, the subject title, the minimum tip material status key in a window of 3 preceding and 1 following row ordered by the number of enrolled students, the responsible faculty name, and the offer department name from the subject offered table? Do not return any rounded answers."
