, `TIP_SUBJECT_OFFERED`, `STUDENT_DEPARTMENT`, `LIBRARY_RESERVE_MATRL_DETAIL`, `TIP_DETAIL`.\n- `dw_4287` ← `LIBRARY_RESERVE_MATRL_DETAIL`, `TIP_DETAIL`, `TIP_SUBJECT_OFFERED`, `ACADEMIC_TERMS_ALL`, `ACADEMIC_TERM_PARAMETER`.\n- `dw_3356` ← `TIP_SUBJECT_OFFERED`, `SIS_DEPARTMENT`, `SIS_SUBJECT_CODE`, `LIBRARY_RESERVE_MATRL_DETAIL`, `TIP_DETAIL`, **`SUBJECT_OFFERED_SUMMARY`**.\n- `dw_3311` ← `SIS_COURSE_DESCRIPTION`, `SIS_SUBJECT_CODE`, `CIS_COURSE_CATALOG`, `LIBRARY_SUBJECT_OFFERED`, `LIBRARY_RESERVE_MATRL_DETAIL`.\n- `dw_3644` / `dw_1212` / `dw_4527` ← `SIS_DEPARTMENT` + `SUBJECT_OFFERED_SUMMARY` for `AVG/STDDEV/VARIANCE(TOTAL_UNITS)` with `TOTAL_UNITS > 0 AND NUM_ENROLLED_STUDENTS >= 1` filters.\n- `dw_2737` / `dw_3131` / `dw_2580` / `dw_3985` ← the HIGH/LOW/AVERAGE classification template.\n\n---\n\n## 3. Similar-Entity Differences\n\n### 3a. Objective dimension matrix\n\n| Dimension | `SUBJECT_OFFERED_SUMMARY` | `SUBJECT_SUMMARY` | `TIP_SUBJECT_OFFERED` | `LIBRARY_SUBJECT_OFFERED` | `SUBJECT_OFFERED` | `COURSE_CATALOG_SUBJECT_OFFERED` |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| Granularity | one row per subject per term (retrieved `default_granularity`) | one row per subject/cluster per term | one row per subject per term **in textbook-program scope** | one row per subject per term **in library-reserve scope** | one row per **section** per term | one row per catalog offering per year/term |\n| `TOTAL_UNITS` | **present** (`column_concept_total_units` member) | present | absent (no unit columns in retrieved `columns`) | absent | present | present |\n| `NUM_ENROLLED_STUDENTS` | **present**, subject grain (`column_concept_enrollment_measures`: \"per subject per term\") | uses `SUBJECT_ENROLLMENT_NUMBER` (official registrar) | present, **program-scope snapshot** | present, **program-scope snapshot** | present, **section grain** | absent |\n| `IS_DEGREE_GRANTING` | absent | absent | absent | absent | absent | absent — only `SIS_COURSE_DESCRIPTION` has it (retrieved columns) |\n| Dept code column | `OFFER_DEPT_CODE` | `DEPARTMENT_CODE`-family | `OFFER_DEPT_CODE` | `OFFER_DEPT_CODE` | `OFFER_DEPT_CODE` | `DEPARTMENT_CODE` |\n| Coverage caveat | full registrar subject population | full | \"may not cover all subjects\" (`column_concept_enrollment_measures`) | \"may not cover all subjects\" | needs aggregation to subject grain | catalog-declared, not actual |\n| Fan-out risk | `COURSE_NUMBER` join to `SIS_COURSE_DESCRIPTION.COURSE` is many-to-one per term row | — | `SUBJECT_ID` join to `TIP_DETAIL` is 1:N (materials per subject) | `SUBJECT_ID` join to `LIBRARY_RESERVE_MATRL_DETAIL` 1:N | section→subject fan-in | `HASS_ATTRIBUTE`-style multi-match documented for catalog lookups |\n\n| Dimension | `SIS_SUBJECT_CODE` | `SIS_COURSE_DESCRIPTION` | `SIS_DEPARTMENT` | `STUDENT_DEPARTMENT` |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| Provides `DEPARTMENT_CODE` + `DEPARTMENT_NAME` | **both present** (retrieved columns) | `DEPARTMENT` + `DEPARTMENT_NAME` | both present | both present |\n| Provides `IS_DEGREE_GRANTING` | absent | **present** ('Y'/'N') | present | absent (per `concept_department_dimension`: attribute coverage differs) |\n| Grain | one row per subject code / course number | one row per course description | one row per department | one row per department |\n| Documented role | \"link courses to departments via DEPARTMENT_CODE\" | \"Joins to SIS_SUBJECT_CODE via COURSE = SUBJECT_CODE/COURSE_NUMBER\" | dimension | student-facing reporting variant |\n\n| Dimension | `LIBRARY_MATERIAL_STATUS_KEY` | `TIP_MATERIAL_STATUS_KEY` |\n|---|---|---|\n| Domain | library reserve (6 values) | textbook program (12 values) |\n| 'U' meaning | Unknown (library) | Unknown (TIP) — **independent domains** |\n| Documented caveat | `column_concept_material_status_key`: \"The two key domains are independent and must not be joined to each other\"; equality \"only matches on coincidental code overlap\" | same |\n\n### 3b. Task-Requirement Fitness Mapping\n\nAtomic requirements decomposed from the question:\n\n| # | Requirement | `SIS_SUBJECT_CODE` | `SIS_COURSE_DESCRIPTION` | `SUBJECT_OFFERED_SUMMARY` | `LIBRARY_RESERVE_MATRL_DETAIL` | `TIP_DETAIL` | `TIP_SUBJECT_OFFERED` | `LIBRARY_SUBJECT_OFFERED` | `SIS_DEPARTMENT` |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| R1 | output department code | **SUPPORTED** (`DEPARTMENT_CODE`) | partial (`DEPARTMENT`) | partial (`OFFER_DEPT_CODE`) | NOT-SUPPORTED | NOT-SUPPORTED | partial (`OFFER_DEPT_CODE`) | partial | SUPPORTED |\n| R2 | output department name | **SUPPORTED** (`DEPARTMENT_NAME`) | SUPPORTED | SUPPORTED (`OFFER_DEPT_NAME`) | NOT-SUPPORTED | NOT-SUPPORTED | SUPPORTED | SUPPORTED | SUPPORTED |\n| R3 | `VARIANCE(TOTAL_UNITS)` | NOT-SUPPORTED (no units) | NOT-SUPPORTED | **SUPPORTED** (`TOTAL_UNITS`) | NOT-SUPPORTED | NOT-SUPPORTED | NOT-SUPPORTED | NOT-SUPPORTED | NOT-SUPPORTED |\n| R4 | `AVG(NUM_ENROLLED_STUDENTS)` at subject grain | NOT-SUPPORTED | NOT-SUPPORTED | **SUPPORTED** | NOT-SUPPORTED | NOT-SUPPORTED | SUPPORTED (program scope only) | SUPPORTED (program scope only) | NOT-SUPPORTED |\n| R5 | degree-granting filter | NOT-SUPPORTED | **SUPPORTED** (`IS_DEGREE_GRANTING`) | NOT-SUPPORTED | NOT-SUPPORTED | NOT-SUPPORTED | NOT-SUPPORTED | NOT-SUPPORTED | SUPPORTED (dept-level, not subject-level → VIOLATES \"degree-granting **subjects**\") |\n| R6 | \"> 0 enrolled students\" filter | NOT-SUPPORTED | NOT-SUPPORTED | **SUPPORTED** | NOT-SUPPORTED | NOT-SUPPORTED | SUPPORTED | SUPPORTED | NOT-SUPPORTED |\n| R7 | library reserve detail rows with status 'U' + 4 output keys | NOT-SUPPORTED | NOT-SUPPORTED | NOT-SUPPORTED | **SUPPORTED** | NOT-SUPPORTED | NOT-SUPPORTED | NOT-SUPPORTED (lacks `LIBRARY_RESERVE_CATALOG_KEY`/`LIBRARY_COURSE_INSTRUCTOR_KEY`) | NOT-SUPPORTED |\n| R8 | tip material key / status key / ISBN | NOT-SUPPORTED | NOT-SUPPORTED | NOT-SUPPORTED | NOT-SUPPORTED | **SUPPORTED** | NOT-SUPPORTED | NOT-SUPPORTED | NOT-SUPPORTED |\n| R9 | subject title, responsible faculty name, offer dept name \"from the subject offered table\" | NOT-SUPPORTED | NOT-SUPPORTED | SUPPORTED | NOT-SUPPORTED | NOT-SUPPORTED | **SUPPORTED** (precedents `dw_3868`/`dw_4287` source these from `TIP_SUBJECT_OFFERED` in the identical column sequence) | SUPPORTED | NOT-SUPPORTED |\n| R10 | window `MIN(TIP_MATERIAL_STATUS_KEY)` ordered by enrolled students | NOT-SUPPORTED | NOT-SUPPORTED | NOT-SUPPORTED | NOT-SUPPORTED | SUPPORTED (measure) | **SUPPORTED** (`NUM_ENROLLED_STUDENTS` ordering key, per `dw_3868`/`dw_4287`) | SUPPORTED | NOT-SUPPORTED |\n| R11 | \"subjects offered by that department\" linkage | SUPPORTED (`DEPARTMENT_CODE`) | SUPPORTED (`COURSE`) | **SUPPORTED** (`OFFER_DEPT_CODE`) | NOT-SUPPORTED | NOT-SUPPORTED | SUPPORTED (`OFFER_DEPT_CODE`) | SUPPORTED | SUPPORTED |\n\n### 3c. Wording-to-Field Anchoring\n\n- **\"department code\" / \"department name\"** → the provided mapping anchors these to `SIS_SUBJECT_CODE.DEPARTMENT_CODE` / `.DEPARTMENT_NAME`. Excludes `SIS_COURSE_DESCRIPTION.DEPT_NAME_IN_COMMENCEMENT_BK`, `SIS_DEPARTMENT.DEPARTMENT_FULL_NAME`, `TIP_SUBJECT_OFFERED.OFFER_DEPT_NAME` (the latter is separately requested as *\"offer department name from the subject offered table\"* — a distinct output slot).\n- **\"variance of the total number of units\"** → `VARIANCE(SUBJECT_OFFERED_SUMMARY.TOTAL_UNITS)`. `column_concept_total_units` decision guide: *\"Unit statistics at subject-offering rollup level with offering department/school → Use SUBJECT_OFFERED_SUMMARY.TOTAL_UNITS.\"* Excludes `COURSE_CATALOG_SUBJECT_OFFERED.TOTAL_UNITS` (catalog-declared) and `SUBJECT_SUMMARY.TOTAL_UNITS` (tied to enrollment-record statistics).\n- **\"degree-granting subjects\"** → `SIS_COURSE_DESCRIPTION.IS_DEGREE_GRANTING = 'Y'`. This is a **subject/course-level** flag; `SIS_DEPARTMENT.IS_DEGREE_GRANTING` is a **department-level** flag used by `dw_3356`/`dw_4527`/`dw_1212` for \"departments that grant degrees\". The question says \"degree-granting **subjects**\", and the gold-table list includes `SIS_COURSE_DESCRIPTION` but **not** `SIS_DEPARTMENT` — this discriminates decisively toward `SIS_COURSE_DESCRIPTION.IS_DEGREE_GRANTING`.\n- **\"more than 0 enrolled students\"** → `SUBJECT_OFFERED_SUMMARY.NUM_ENROLLED_STUDENTS > 0`. Precedent `dw_1212`/`dw_3644` use `NUM_ENROLLED_STUDENTS >= 1` with `TOTAL_UNITS > 0` on the same table; `dw_3311` uses `NUM_ENROLLED_STUDENTS > 0` on `LIBRARY_SUBJECT_OFFERED`. The mapping anchors \"enrolled students\" to `SUBJECT_OFFERED_SUMMARY.NUM_ENROLLED_STUDENTS`.\n- **\"subjects offered by that department\"** → the mapping anchors this to `SUBJECT_OFFERED_SUMMARY.OFFER_DEPT_CODE`. Discriminating fact: `SIS_SUBJECT_CODE.DEPARTMENT_CODE`, `SUBJECT_OFFERED_SUMMARY.OFFER_DEPT_CODE` and `TIP_SUBJECT_OFFERED.OFFER_DEPT_CODE` all share the same department-code domain (each documented as joining `SIS_DEPARTMENT.DEPARTMENT_CODE`), so equating them is a valid cross-table key.\n- **\"material status key equal to 'U'\"** → `LIBRARY_RESERVE_MATRL_DETAIL.LIBRARY_MATERIAL_STATUS_KEY = 'U'` (library domain), **not** `TIP_DETAIL.TIP_MATERIAL_STATUS_KEY = 'U'` — `column_concept_material_status_key` explicitly forbids equating the two.\n- **\"the subject title … the responsible faculty name, and the offer department name from the subject offered table\"** → `TIP_SUBJECT_OFFERED.SUBJECT_TITLE / .RESPONSIBLE_FACULTY_NAME / .OFFER_DEPT_NAME`. Discriminating evidence: `dw_3868` and `dw_4287` produce this *exact* column sequence (instructor key, catalog key, term code, subject ID, tip material key, tip material status key, ISBN, subject title, windowed min status, responsible faculty name, offer dept name) sourcing all of them from `TIP_SUBJECT_OFFERED` in the identical library-reserve join chain.\n- **\"minimum tip material status key in a window of 3 preceding and 1 following row ordered by the number of enrolled students\"** → `MIN(TIP_DETAIL.TIP_MATERIAL_STATUS_KEY) OVER (ORDER BY <enrolled> ROWS BETWEEN 3 PRECEDING AND 1 FOLLOWING)`. The mapping anchors the ordering measure to `SUBJECT_OFFERED_SUMMARY.NUM_ENROLLED_STUDENTS`, but the two precedents with this verbatim window (`dw_3868`, `dw_4287`) both order by `TIP_SUBJECT_OFFERED.NUM_ENROLLED_STUDENTS` inside the same `LIBRARY_RESERVE_MATRL_DETAIL ⋈ TIP_DETAIL ⋈ TIP_SUBJECT_OFFERED` chain. Discriminating fact: the window must be evaluated over the material-detail row set, which only exists in that chain; `SUBJECT_OFFERED_SUMMARY` is not part of it.\n- **\"overall average\"** (for the 20% category) → ambiguous between *average of departmental averages* and *row-level average over the joined population*. Discriminating precedent: `dw_2737` uses the **verbatim** template \"at least 20% greater than the overall average … or 'AVERAGE'\" and computes `CROSS JOIN (SELECT AVG(d.MAX_ENROLLMENT) … WHERE <same filters>)` — a **row-level AVG over the filtered population**, not an average of group averages. `dw_3131` (average of group variances) is worded differently (\"the average variance across all periods\"). Per the task tip's exception clause, the row-level precedent governs.\n\n### 3d. Precedent Usage Evidence\n\n- **`LIBRARY_RESERVE_MATRL_DETAIL ⋈ TIP_DETAIL ⋈ TIP_SUBJECT_OFFERED` on `SUBJECT_ID`, filtered `LIBRARY_MATERIAL_STATUS_KEY='U'`, with `MIN(TIP_MATERIAL_STATUS_KEY) OVER (ORDER BY NUM_ENROLLED_STUDENTS ROWS BETWEEN 3 PRECEDING AND 1 FOLLOWING)`**: 2 precedents — `dw_3868`, `dw_4287`. Both emit the identical 11-column tail requested here.\n- **`VARIANCE(TOTAL_UNITS)` / `AVG(NUM_ENROLLED_STUDENTS)` on `SUBJECT_OFFERED_SUMMARY` grouped by department with `IS_DEGREE_GRANTING` + enrollment filters**: 4 precedents — `dw_1212` (`AVG`+`STDDEV`, `TOTAL_UNITS>0 AND NUM_ENROLLED_STUDENTS>=1`), `dw_3644` (same filters), `dw_4527` (`VARIANCE`+`STDDEV` of `NUM_ENROLLED_STUDENTS`), `dw_3356` (`VARIANCE`+`STDDEV`, degree-granting departments).\n- **Degree-granting flag source**: `SIS_COURSE_DESCRIPTION.IS_DEGREE_GRANTING` — precedents `dw_2924`, `dw_3163`, `dw_1766`, `dw_1692`, `dw_2272`, `dw_1335` (course/subject-level); `SIS_DEPARTMENT.IS_DEGREE_GRANTING` — precedents `dw_3356`, `dw_4527`, `dw_1212`, `dw_1350`, `dw_3727`, `dw_3237`, `dw_4231`, `dw_4490`, `dw_4234` (department-level). Frequencies reported; the question's wording \"degree-granting **subjects**\" plus the gold-table list (which contains `SIS_COURSE_DESCRIPTION` and not `SIS_DEPARTMENT`) is the discriminating fact.\n- **HIGH/LOW/AVERAGE 20%-threshold classification**: 3 precedents — `dw_2737` (row-level overall AVG, wording \"the overall average\"), `dw_3131` (AVG of group variances, wording \"the average variance across all periods\"), `dw_2580` (AVG of group counts per year, wording \"the average across all departments for that year\"). 1 additional precedent with the exact `HIGH_ENROLLMENT`/`LOW_ENROLLMENT`/`AVERAGE` labels at a 10% threshold against a *group* average: `dw_3985`.\n- **`SIS_SUBJECT_CODE ⋈ SIS_COURSE_DESCRIPTION` on `COURSE = COURSE_NUMBER`**: precedents `dw_3311`, `dw_3356`, `dw_4527`, `dw_3985`.\n\n---\n\n## 4. Business Usage\n\n- **`LIBRARY_RESERVE_MATRL_DETAIL`** — consumed by 20+ metrics (`dw_3868`, `dw_4287`, `dw_3311`, `dw_3356`, `dw_2850`, `dw_2895`, `dw_4583`, `dw_4826`, `dw_4701`, `dw_4978`, `dw_3357`, `dw_4458`, `dw_4566`, `dw_3234`, `dw_3664`, `dw_4812`, …). Serves \"which subjects have reserve materials / of what status\" questions; the `'U'` (Unknown) filter is the single most recurring predicate in this family.\n- **`TIP_DETAIL` + `TIP_SUBJECT_OFFERED`** — the textbook-program pair; `TIP_SUBJECT_OFFERED` supplies subject title, offering dept/school, responsible faculty and enrollment for material-level reports; `TIP_DETAIL` supplies material key/status/ISBN. `concept_course_material_programs` documents them as jointly answering \"which subjects have course materials/textbooks\".\n- **`SUBJECT_OFFERED_SUMMARY`** — 39 dependent metrics; the canonical source for per-department unit and enrollment dispersion (`AVG`/`VARIANCE`/`STDDEV` of `TOTAL_UNITS`, `NUM_ENROLLED_STUDENTS`) at subject grain with offering-department attribution.\n- **`SIS_SUBJECT_CODE` + `SIS_COURSE_DESCRIPTION`** — the SIS catalog pair: `SIS_SUBJECT_CODE` resolves course numbers to department code/name; `SIS_COURSE_DESCRIPTION` supplies course level, degree-granting flag and CIP code. Used together in `dw_3311`, `dw_3356`, `dw_4527`, `dw_3985`.\n- **`LIBRARY_SUBJECT_OFFERED`** — the library-program parent; used when the question needs library-scope enrollment/course-number descriptions (`dw_3311`, `dw_3393`, `dw_3911`, `dw_1221`, `dw_4724`). Not needed here because the requested title/faculty/dept-name come \"from the subject offered table\" in the TIP chain per the precedent column sequence.\n- **`SIS_DEPARTMENT` / `STUDENT_DEPARTMENT`** — department dimension used when school attribution, full name, budget code or the department-level degree-granting flag is required (`dw_3868`, `dw_1350`, `dw_1288`).\n\n---\n\n## 5. Coverage Checklist\n\n| Entity | Tools called |\n|---|---|\n| `SIS_SUBJECT_CODE` | `semantic_search` ×2, `semantic_get`, `semantic_graph query_neighbors(both)` |\n| `SIS_COURSE_DESCRIPTION` | `semantic_search` ×2, `semantic_get`, appeared in `SIS_SUBJECT_CODE` neighbor traversal |\n| `SUBJECT_OFFERED_SUMMARY` | `semantic_search` ×3, `semantic_get`, `semantic_graph metrics_by_table` (39 metrics) |\n| `LIBRARY_RESERVE_MATRL_DETAIL` | `semantic_search` ×2, `semantic_get`, `semantic_graph query_neighbors(both)` (14 edges) |\n| `TIP_DETAIL` | `semantic_search` ×2, `semantic_get` |\n| `TIP_SUBJECT_OFFERED` | `semantic_search` ×2, `semantic_get`, neighbor traversal |\n| `LIBRARY_SUBJECT_OFFERED`, `LIBRARY_RESERVE_CATALOG`, `LIBRARY_COURSE_INSTRUCTOR`, `LIBRARY_MATERIAL_STATUS`, `TIP_MATERIAL`, `TIP_MATERIAL_STATUS` | `semantic_search`, neighbor traversal of `LIBRARY_RESERVE_MATRL_DETAIL`, `concept_course_material_programs` membership |\n| `SIS_DEPARTMENT`, `STUDENT_DEPARTMENT`, `SIS_ADMIN_DEPARTMENT` | `semantic_search`, `concept_department_dimension`, precedent SQL inspection |\n| `SUBJECT_SUMMARY`, `SUBJECT_OFFERED`, `COURSE_CATALOG_SUBJECT_OFFERED`, `CIS_COURSE_CATALOG`, `DRUPAL_COURSE_CATALOG` | `semantic_search` ×3, `column_concept_total_units`, `column_concept_enrollment_measures`, precedent SQL |\n| `ACADEMIC_TERMS`, `ACADEMIC_TERMS_ALL` | `semantic_search`, neighbor traversal (no term attribute requested → unused) |\n| Facilities/space/HR/Moira/time/person/CIP/IAP tables (`FCLT_*`, `FAC_*`, `SPACE_*`, `HR_*`, `MASTER_DEPT_*`, `MOIRA_*`, `TIME_*`, `CIP*`, `IAP_*`, `EMPLOYEE_DIRECTORY`, `OPA_PERSON_CURRENT`, `MIT_STUDENT_DIRECTORY`, `HR_FACULTY_ROSTER`, `SE_PERSON`, `ZPM_ROOMS_LOAD`, `BUILDINGS`, etc.) | `semantic_search` (returned), screened: no requested measure/key/filter column resides only in them |\n| Concepts: `concept_course_material_programs`, `concept_subject_offering_facts`, `concept_department_dimension`, `concept_course_catalog_sources`, `concept_academic_term_dimension`, `concept_person_directory`, `concept_cip_program_classification`, `concept_iap_activities`, `concept_time_dimension`, `concept_dept_hr_org_hierarchy`, `concept_building_inventory`, `concept_room_space_inventory`, `concept_space_unit_dimension`, `concept_room_major_use_classification`, `concept_floor_inventory`, `concept_facility_organization_dimension`, `concept_building_address`, `concept_moira_mailing_lists` | `semantic_search`, `semantic_get` (first one in full) |\n| Column-concepts: `material_status_key`, `enrollment_measures`, `total_units`, `department_name`, `subject_id`, `term_code`, `master_subject_id`, `year_columns`, and the facilities/space/person ones | `semantic_search`, `semantic_get` (first four in full) |\n| Metrics `dw_3868`, `dw_4287`, `dw_3311`, `dw_3356`, `dw_4527`, `dw_1212`, `dw_3644`, `dw_1350`, `dw_2958`, `dw_2737`, `dw_3131`, `dw_2580`, `dw_3985` | `semantic_get` (full SQL retrieved) |\n| Remaining ~100 metrics listed in §1 | `semantic_search` desc-level retrieval; screened for shape relevance |\n| `mysql_query` | **Attempted 6× — all failed with `1045 (28000): Access denied for user 'root'@'localhost'`.** No data-level verification was possible; all claims above are sourced from `semantic_get` / `semantic_graph` content only. |\n\n---\n\n## 6. Recommendation\n\n### 6a. Recommended tables/columns\n\n| Role | Choice | Justification (evidence) |\n|---|---|---|\n| Department code / name | `SIS_SUBJECT_CODE.DEPARTMENT_CODE`, `.DEPARTMENT_NAME` | Task mapping; `SIS_SUBJECT_CODE` documented as \"link courses to departments via DEPARTMENT_CODE\" (§1). |\n| Degree-granting filter | `SIS_COURSE_DESCRIPTION.IS_DEGREE_GRANTING = 'Y'` | Only table in the gold set carrying a subject/course-level degree-granting flag (§3b R5); `SIS_DEPARTMENT` is not a gold table here. |\n| Unit variance & enrollment average | `VARIANCE(SUBJECT_OFFERED_SUMMARY.TOTAL_UNITS)`, `AVG(SUBJECT_OFFERED_SUMMARY.NUM_ENROLLED_STUDENTS)` | `column_concept_total_units` decision guide + `column_concept_enrollment_measures` (subject grain); precedents `dw_1212`, `dw_3644`, `dw_4527` (§3d). |\n| \"Subjects offered by that department\" | `SUBJECT_OFFERED_SUMMARY.OFFER_DEPT_CODE = SIS_SUBJECT_CODE.DEPARTMENT_CODE` | Task mapping anchors the phrase to this column; all three `OFFER_DEPT_CODE`/`DEPARTMENT_CODE` columns are documented against the same `SIS_DEPARTMENT.DEPARTMENT_CODE` domain (§3c). |\n| Enrollment filter | `SUBJECT_OFFERED_SUMMARY.NUM_ENROLLED_STUDENTS > 0` | Mapping + precedent `dw_3311` (`> 0`), `dw_1212`/`dw_3644` (`>= 1`). |\n| Reserve-material rows | `LIBRARY_RESERVE_MATRL_DETAIL` with `LIBRARY_MATERIAL_STATUS_KEY = 'U'`; output `LIBRARY_COURSE_INSTRUCTOR_KEY`, `LIBRARY_RESERVE_CATALOG_KEY`, `TERM_CODE`, `SUBJECT_ID` | `column_concept_material_status_key` decision guide; precedents `dw_3868`, `dw_4287`. |\n| Textbook attributes | `TIP_DETAIL.TIP_MATERIAL_KEY`, `.TIP_MATERIAL_STATUS_KEY`, `.ISBN`, joined `LIBRARY_RESERVE_MATRL_DETAIL.SUBJECT_ID = TIP_DETAIL.SUBJECT_ID` | Task join keys; `concept_course_material_programs` decision guide. |\n| Title / faculty / offer dept name / window ordering | `TIP_SUBJECT_OFFERED.SUBJECT_TITLE`, `.RESPONSIBLE_FACULTY_NAME`, `.OFFER_DEPT_NAME`, `.NUM_ENROLLED_STUDENTS`, joined `TIP_DETAIL.SUBJECT_ID = TIP_SUBJECT_OFFERED.SUBJECT_ID` | Verbatim precedent column sequence in `dw_3868` and `dw_4287` (§3c, §3d). |\n| Window | `MIN(TIP_MATERIAL_STATUS_KEY) OVER (ORDER BY NUM_ENROLLED_STUDENTS ROWS BETWEEN 3 PRECEDING AND 1 FOLLOWING)` | Identical expression in both precedents. |\n| Category thresholds | `> overall * 1.2` → `HIGH_ENROLLMENT`; `< overall * 0.8` → `LOW_ENROLLMENT`; else `AVERAGE` | `dw_2737` uses exactly `* 1.2` / `* 0.8` for the same \"at least 20% higher/lower than the overall average\" wording. |\n| \"Overall average\" | row-level `AVG(NUM_ENROLLED_STUDENTS)` over the same filtered, joined degree-granting population | `dw_2737` precedent + task tip exception clause (§3c). |\n\n### 6b. Recommended SQL writing approach\n\nThree CTEs:\n1. **`dept_stats`** — `SIS_SUBJECT_CODE ⋈ SIS_COURSE_DESCRIPTION (COURSE = COURSE_NUMBER) ⋈ SUBJECT_OFFERED_SUMMARY (COURSE = COURSE_NUMBER AND OFFER_DEPT_CODE = DEPARTMENT_CODE)`, filters `IS_DEGREE_GRANTING='Y'` and `NUM_ENROLLED_STUDENTS > 0`, `GROUP BY DEPARTMENT_CODE, DEPARTMENT_NAME`, emitting `VARIANCE(TOTAL_UNITS)` and `AVG(NUM_ENROLLED_STUDENTS)`.\n2. **`library_reserve_materials`** — the `dw_3868`/`dw_4287` chain, evaluated *before* any department join so the window frame spans the full status-'U' material population (exactly as both precedents do). It also carries `TIP_SUBJECT_OFFERED.OFFER_DEPT_CODE` for the department linkage.\n3. **`overall`** — the same joins/filters as `dept_stats` without grouping, yielding the row-level `AVG(NUM_ENROLLED_STUDENTS)`.\n\nFinal: `dept_stats JOIN library_reserve_materials ON DEPARTMENT_CODE = OFFER_DEPT_CODE CROSS JOIN overall`, with the `CASE` category. No `ROUND()` anywhere (\"Do not